---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy Policy | KenLens — 研レンズ"
  description="Privacy policy for the KenLens Chrome extension: what information is sent, what is stored locally, and what is never collected."
  path="en/privacy/"
  alternatePath="privacy/"
>
  <Header lang="en" path="privacy/" />
  <main>
    <article class="container prose">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="effective-date">Effective date: June 10, 2026</p>

      <p>
        KenLens (研レンズ, "the extension") is a Chrome extension that displays public
        metadata on researcher pages of researchmap.jp. This policy explains what
        information the extension handles.
      </p>

      <h2>Information that leaves your browser</h2>
      <p>
        The extension communicates with external servers only when needed to process
        the researchmap page you are viewing or to check its operational configuration.
        Specifically:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          When you view a researchmap researcher page, the extension sends the
          profile permalink to api.researchmap.jp to fetch the publicly available
          publication data.
        </li>
        <li>
          For each publication, the extension sends the DOI to OpenAlex, Crossref,
          and Unpaywall to fetch public metadata such as citation counts and OA
          status. For DOI-less papers with Latin-script titles, Crossref receives
          only the paper title and the developer's contact email address for
          DOI-candidate matching. Publication year and author family name are used
          only for matching inside your browser and are not sent to Crossref.
        </li>
        <li>
          In the maintenance report, KenLens also queries OpenAlex for the author's
          works using the OpenAlex author-record ID derived from those DOIs. It also
          sends only the researchmap permalink to api.researchmap.jp to fetch public
          lists of published papers, MISC items, books and other works, and
          presentations or talks for matching. BibTeX files you paste or select are
          processed entirely inside your browser and never transmitted.
        </li>
        <li>
          About once a day, the extension fetches an operational configuration file
          (config.json) from the developer's GitHub Pages site (r-okauchi.github.io).
          This file is a kill switch for researchmap API usage, and the request
          contains no personal information or browsing information.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        No other information leaves your browser: no browsing history, no activity on
        other websites, and no personally identifying information.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we never collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No account or sign-in is required, and users are not identified.</li>
        <li>No analytics are used.</li>
        <li>Browsing history is never collected.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Information stored locally</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Responses from external APIs are cached inside your browser
          (chrome.storage.local) to speed up display. Cache lifetimes range from
          24 hours to 30 days depending on the content, and the cache can be cleared
          at any time from the options page.
        </li>
        <li>
          An optional, user-supplied OpenAlex API key is stored locally only and is
          used solely for requests to OpenAlex. It is never sent anywhere else.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Scope</h2>
      <p>The extension runs only on researchmap.jp pages.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about this policy, please use
        <a href="https://github.com/R-Okauchi/kenlens/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          GitHub Issues
        </a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        This policy may be updated from time to time. Significant changes will be
        announced on this page.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer lang="en" />
</Base>
